==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|heimskr||foolish, silly; who has never been from home|lang=non}}, from {{term|heima||home|lang=is}}.

===Adjective===
{{is-adj-01|heimsk|heimskt|heimskari|heimskastur}}

# [[stupid]], [[foolish]], [[dumb]]
#: ''Ógn er hann '''heimskur'''.''
#:: Oh how very '''stupid''' he is.
#: ''Að gera einhvern '''heimskan'''.'' (''synonym:'' {{term|forheimska|lang=is}})
#:: To '''stultify''' someone.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|heimskt er heimaalið barn}} (travel broadens the mind; homish is the home-bred bairn)

====Related terms====
